        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Highly-compensated employees (i.e., the highest paid 10% of salaried employees within 75 miles of the employee's worksite) may not be returned to their former or equivalent position following a leave if restoration of employment will cause substantial and grievous economic injury to the Company. The Company on a case-by-case basis will make this fact-specific determination. The Company will notify you if you qualify as a \"highly compensated\" employee, if the Company intends to deny reinstatement, and of your rights in such instances.",
